7, "text": "During his tenure at Harvard Medical School, Gatti contributed to several seminal studies that shed light on the intricate relationships between human health, environmental degradation, and evolutionary adaptation."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1088, "end": 1272, "text": "One of his most notable works, published in the journal Nature in 2008, explored the impact of climate change on the evolution of disease vectors and its implications for human health."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1273, "end": 1276, "text": "[1]"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1278, "end": 1482, "text": "In addition to his research endeavors, Gatti also taught courses on environmental health and evolutionary medicine at Harvard Medical School, earning him recognition as an exceptional educator and mentor."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1483, "end": 1515, "text": "Notable Studies and Publications"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1517, "end": 1528, "text": "* Gatti, R."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1529, "end": 1539, "text": "C., et al."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1540, "end": 1547, "text": "(2008)."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1548, "end": 1628, "text": "\"Climate change and the evolution of disease vectors: A review of the evidence.\""}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1629, "end": 1656, "text": "Nature, 452(7185), 171-175."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1657, "end": 1682, "text": "doi: 10.1038\\/nature06734"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1683, "end": 1694, "text": "* Gatti, R."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1695, "end": 1710, "text": "C., & Smith, J."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1711, "end": 1718, "text": "(2009